# TrendPilot.Backend

`TrendPilot.Backend` is an ASP.NET Core app on .NET 10. A Business or Creator Instagram account signs in through official Instagram Business Login, and the app reads that account.

## Keep this file current

Edit this file in the same change when any of these happen:

- A route is added, removed, or its response shape changes.
- A type moves, or a new project or folder takes over one of the three roles.
- Session storage changes, including replacing the single in-memory login.
- The redirect URI, Graph version, host, port, or where the app id and secret are read changes.
- Instagram request or response shape changes, including token parsing.

Replace the old fact. Do not append a changelog. Do not write the app id, app secret, or access token into this file.

## Architecture

Three roles live in one process.

- HTTP edge: `Program.cs`. Maps routes, checks the session, and chooses status codes. It does not know Instagram URL shapes.
- Instagram adapter: `InstagramClient` in `InstagramClient.cs`. Builds the authorize URL, exchanges the code, and loads profile and media. It returns `InstagramResult<T>` (a value, or a status plus an error). Routes turn that into the HTTP response.
- Memory: `InstagramSessionStore` in `InstagramClient.cs`. One process-wide login (`userId`, token, expiry) and short-lived `state` values used once. A restart clears both. There is no database.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Browser
    participant Routes as Program.cs
    participant Store as InstagramSessionStore
    participant Client as InstagramClient
    participant Instagram
    Browser->>Routes: GET /instagram/login
    Routes->>Store: CreateState
    Routes->>Client: BuildAuthorizeUrl
    Routes->>Browser: redirect
    Instagram->>Routes: GET /instagram/callback
    Routes->>Store: TryConsumeState
    Routes->>Client: ExchangeCodeAsync
    Client->>Instagram: short-lived token then 60-day token
    Routes->>Store: Set login
    Browser->>Routes: GET /instagram/me
    Routes->>Store: GetValid
    Routes->>Client: GetAccountAsync
    Client->>Instagram: profile and one page of media
    Routes->>Browser: InstagramAccount
```

The browser receives `InstagramProfile`, `InstagramMedia`, and `InstagramAccount`. Instagram field names stay inside `InstagramClient`.

## Boundaries

- New HTTP behavior goes in `Program.cs`. New Instagram URLs, fields, and token parsing stay in `InstagramClient`.
- Do not put the access token in a response, a log, or `appsettings.json`.
- Keep official Instagram Business Login. Do not add scraping or a route that takes an arbitrary page id.
- Short-lived token JSON may be a `data` array or a flat object with `access_token` and numeric `user_id`.
- The session is one in-memory login. A feature that needs many users must replace `InstagramSessionStore` on purpose, not by adding a second global token.

## Files

- `TrendPilot.Backend.csproj` sets assembly name `TrendPilot.Backend` and root namespace `TrendPilot.Backend`.
- `Program.cs` maps the routes.
- `InstagramClient.cs` holds the client, session store, and response types.
- `appsettings.json` holds `Instagram:GraphVersion` (`v25.0`) and `Instagram:RedirectUri` (`https://localhost:7061/instagram/callback`).
- `Properties/launchSettings.json` is local launch only. It sets the listen addresses and the `Instagram__AppId` and `Instagram__AppSecret` environment variables.

## Routes

- `GET /` returns `Hello World!`.
- `GET /instagram/login` stores a one-time `state` and redirects to Instagram with scope `instagram_business_basic`.
- `GET /instagram/callback` checks `state`, exchanges the code, stores the login, and returns `{ signedIn, userId }`.
- `GET /instagram/me` returns the signed-in profile and one page of media. With no session it returns 401.

## Configuration

The app id and secret come from `Instagram__AppId` and `Instagram__AppSecret`. Locally those are set in the launch profile. In production the host environment sets them. The Meta OAuth redirect URI must match `https://localhost:7061/instagram/callback` exactly for local login.

## Run

From the `trendpilot` folder:

```bash
dotnet run --launch-profile http
```

The process listens on `https://localhost:7061` and `http://localhost:5056`.
